{"id":"ux-user-research","title":"UI/UX: user research","subject":"UI/UX design","label":"UI/UX design","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":168,"duration":168.48,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":455,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Start","start":0,"end":18.365},{"id":"explain","title":"The idea","start":18.365,"end":45.295},{"id":"explain2","title":"More methods","start":45.295,"end":95.085},{"id":"example","title":"Example","start":95.085,"end":110.655},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":110.655,"end":121.455},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":121.455,"end":126.895},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Mistakes","start":126.895,"end":146.295},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":146.295,"end":168.48}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.82,"text":"Have you ever built something you thought was clear, then watched someone struggle with it?","w":[0.52,0.66,0.8,1.02,1.3,1.68,1.86,2.1,2.32,3.18,3.42,3.76,4.1,4.44,4.62]},{"s":0,"a":5.27,"b":5.95,"text":"I'm Kora.","w":[5.38,5.56]},{"s":0,"a":6.25,"b":12.12,"text":"In UI and UX design, user research comes before design, because the designer is not the user.","w":[6.3,6.48,6.82,6.96,7.26,8.26,8.54,9.04,9.3,9.62,10.38,10.66,10.78,11.3,11.44,11.64,11.84]},{"s":0,"a":12.42,"b":14.58,"text":"So let's find out what people really need.","w":[12.5,12.68,12.96,13.24,13.42,13.64,14,14.3]},{"s":0,"a":14.88,"b":17.94,"text":"Good design starts with real people, not assumptions.","w":[14.92,15.14,15.64,15.96,16.16,16.42,17.14,17.32]},{"s":1,"a":18.79,"b":22.56,"text":"User research means finding out what people really need before you design.","w":[18.94,19.2,19.68,19.98,20.36,20.5,20.68,21.08,21.44,21.68,21.98,22.1]},{"s":1,"a":22.86,"b":26.52,"text":"Start with research, because your taste and guesses are not evidence.","w":[22.94,23.22,23.42,24.24,24.48,24.66,25.02,25.16,25.62,25.76,26]},{"s":1,"a":26.82,"b":27.93,"text":"Three main methods help.","w":[26.84,27.12,27.36,27.7]},{"s":1,"a":28.23,"b":32.37,"text":"In an interview, you talk to one person at a time and ask open questions.","w":[28.26,28.38,28.5,28.96,29.12,29.36,29.58,29.74,30.1,30.22,30.3,30.88,31.12,31.46,31.72]},{"s":1,"a":32.67,"b":36.2,"text":"Observation means watching people do the task in their real setting.","w":[32.8,33.42,33.72,34.12,34.48,34.66,34.78,35.26,35.36,35.56,35.86]},{"s":1,"a":36.5,"b":38.94,"text":"What people do often differs from what they say.","w":[36.56,36.76,37.1,37.38,37.68,38.04,38.22,38.38,38.6]},{"s":1,"a":39.24,"b":41.91,"text":"Surveys reach many people and are good for counting.","w":[39.34,39.82,40.08,40.34,40.72,40.86,41.02,41.3,41.46]},{"s":1,"a":42.21,"b":44.87,"text":"Surveys are weak for explaining why.","w":[42.88,43.34,43.5,43.78,43.94,44.48]},{"s":2,"a":45.72,"b":50.07,"text":"Qualitative research answers why and how, using words and stories.","w":[45.78,46.42,46.92,47.3,47.7,47.86,48.64,48.94,49.36,49.5]},{"s":2,"a":50.37,"b":53.69,"text":"Quantitative research answers how many, using numbers.","w":[50.42,51.06,51.62,51.94,52.14,52.88,53.14]},{"s":2,"a":53.99,"b":56.87,"text":"Good interview questions are open and about the past.","w":[54.02,54.28,54.66,55.12,55.38,56,56.12,56.34,56.46]},{"s":2,"a":57.17,"b":60.2,"text":"Ask, tell me about the last time you sent money to someone.","w":[57.34,58.02,58.24,58.4,58.62,58.76,59.08,59.3,59.44,59.66,59.9,60.02]},{"s":2,"a":60.5,"b":63.21,"text":"Don't ask, would you use an app that does this?","w":[60.54,60.94,61.5,61.68,61.92,62.06,62.26,62.42,62.58,62.82]},{"s":2,"a":63.66,"b":66.41,"text":"People are bad at predicting their own future behaviour.","w":[63.7,64.06,64.2,64.52,64.62,65.06,65.32,65.56,65.9]},{"s":2,"a":66.71,"b":70.45,"text":"So you learn what actually happened, not what they guess they might do.","w":[66.78,66.94,67.1,67.34,67.6,68,68.9,69.14,69.3,69.48,69.78,69.96,70.18]},{"s":2,"a":70.75,"b":75.52,"text":"Avoid leading questions that suggest the answer, like, don't you find this confusing?","w":[70.8,71.2,71.52,72,72.18,72.58,72.74,73.56,74.22,74.42,74.56,74.78,74.94]},{"s":2,"a":75.97,"b":78.42,"text":"Listen more than you talk, and ask why.","w":[76.04,76.4,76.62,76.74,76.9,77.54,77.8,78.06]},{"s":2,"a":78.72,"b":80.76,"text":"Ask why again when an answer is vague.","w":[78.82,79.06,79.32,79.7,79.86,80.02,80.32,80.42]},{"s":2,"a":81.06,"b":85.56,"text":"After research, group what you heard into patterns and write a short problem statement.","w":[81.16,81.42,82.16,82.46,82.6,82.76,83,83.22,84.04,84.18,84.4,84.5,84.8,85.16]},{"s":2,"a":85.86,"b":91.45,"text":"A persona is a short description of a typical user built from real research, not from imagination.","w":[85.9,85.98,86.54,86.68,86.8,87.06,87.6,87.7,87.76,88.26,88.58,88.88,89.1,89.38,90.26,90.54,90.76]},{"s":2,"a":91.75,"b":94.66,"text":"Five to eight interviews already show the main patterns.","w":[91.8,92.12,92.34,92.6,93.18,93.54,93.76,93.86,94.06]},{"s":3,"a":95.51,"b":96.9,"text":"Here is a worked example.","w":[95.58,95.82,95.96,96.04,96.38]},{"s":3,"a":97.2,"b":101.42,"text":"Turn the leading question, would you like a faster way to pay school fees?","w":[97.26,97.58,97.7,98.04,99.04,99.2,99.32,99.56,99.68,100.14,100.36,100.5,100.7,101]},{"s":3,"a":101.87,"b":106.03,"text":"Into, tell me about the last time you paid school fees. What was hardest?","w":[101.94,102.48,102.68,102.8,103.02,103.16,103.48,103.72,103.86,104.12,104.42,105.2,105.36,105.52]},{"s":3,"a":106.48,"b":110.23,"text":"The first question leads, because it suggests the answer you want.","w":[106.52,106.68,106.98,107.42,108.24,108.54,108.66,109.18,109.42,109.74,109.9]},{"s":4,"a":111.08,"b":113.74,"text":"Quick check. Which is the better interview question?","w":[111.14,111.42,112.18,112.42,112.54,112.68,113,113.34]},{"s":4,"a":114.19,"b":115.53,"text":"Do you like our new design?","w":[114.19,114.28,114.44,114.66,114.82,115]},{"s":4,"a":115.98,"b":118.3,"text":"Or, show me how you would book a ticket?","w":[116.14,116.84,117.1,117.24,117.44,117.56,117.7,117.9,117.96]},{"s":4,"a":118.75,"b":121.03,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[118.8,119.14,119.44,119.62,119.92,120.5,120.68]},{"s":5,"a":121.88,"b":123.26,"text":"The second question is better.","w":[121.92,122.06,122.4,122.84,122.96]},{"s":5,"a":123.56,"b":126.47,"text":"It shows behaviour and does not lead you towards an answer.","w":[123.64,123.78,124.1,124.68,124.9,125.12,125.32,125.54,125.7,126.02,126.14]},{"s":6,"a":127.32,"b":131.52,"text":"Common mistakes: asking friends and family only, so you hear one view.","w":[127.4,127.76,128.68,129.06,129.38,129.52,130,130.3,130.5,130.68,131.02,131.18]},{"s":6,"a":131.82,"b":135.41,"text":"Asking people what features they want, then building that list.","w":[131.94,132.28,132.6,132.84,133.24,133.42,134.14,134.42,134.78,134.98]},{"s":6,"a":135.71,"b":139.44,"text":"Leading questions, and inventing personas without talking to anyone.","w":[135.74,136.06,136.96,137.08,137.58,138.14,138.48,138.86,139.1]},{"s":6,"a":139.74,"b":145.87,"text":"Avoid each by speaking to real users, asking about past behaviour, and building personas from evidence.","w":[139.84,140.26,140.48,140.68,141.02,141.18,141.5,142.28,142.62,142.88,143.16,144,144.2,144.6,145.12,145.34]},{"s":7,"a":146.72,"b":151.49,"text":"Recap. Research comes before design, because the designer is not the user.","w":[146.78,147.7,148.14,148.44,148.78,149.66,149.98,150.08,150.66,150.8,150.98,151.18]},{"s":7,"a":151.79,"b":156.29,"text":"Use interviews, observation, and surveys to learn what people really need.","w":[151.92,152.18,153.02,154,154.2,154.68,154.84,155.08,155.24,155.66,156]},{"s":7,"a":156.59,"b":161.57,"text":"Group patterns, write a problem statement, and build personas from real evidence.","w":[156.64,156.92,157.7,157.94,158.02,158.46,159.28,159.48,159.84,160.44,160.68,161.02]},{"s":7,"a":161.87,"b":165.31,"text":"Top tip: ask about the past, not the future.","w":[161.96,162.26,163.12,163.38,163.62,163.74,164.56,164.76,164.88]},{"s":7,"a":165.61,"b":167.88,"text":"Knowzone is here to help you keep learning.","w":[165.72,166.36,166.5,166.78,166.92,167.12,167.3,167.54]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"UI/UX: user research","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Built something clear but users struggled?"},{"at":6.15,"kind":"term","text":"User research","detail":"Comes before design; designer is not the user."},{"at":14.78,"kind":"text","text":"Good design starts with real people, not assumptions."}]},{"at":18.54,"heading":"User research","items":[{"at":18.69,"kind":"term","text":"User research","detail":"Find out what people need before design."},{"at":22.76,"kind":"text","text":"Research before design: taste/guesses ≠ evidence."},{"at":26.72,"kind":"text","text":"Three main methods."}]},{"at":27.98,"heading":"Three methods","items":[{"at":28.13,"kind":"term","text":"Interviews","detail":"One person at a time; open questions."},{"at":32.57,"kind":"term","text":"Observation","detail":"Watch people do the task in real setting."},{"at":36.4,"kind":"text","text":"What people do ≠ what they say"},{"at":39.14,"kind":"term","text":"Surveys","detail":"Many people; good for counting."},{"at":42.11,"kind":"text","text":"Surveys weak for explaining why."}]},{"at":45.47,"heading":"Qualitative vs quantitative","items":[{"at":45.62,"kind":"term","text":"Qualitative","detail":"Answers why/how; words and stories."},{"at":50.27,"kind":"term","text":"Quantitative","detail":"Answers how many; numbers."},{"at":53.89,"kind":"text","text":"Good interview questions: open + about past."},{"at":57.07,"kind":"text","text":"Ask: 'Tell me about the last time you sent money...'"},{"at":60.4,"kind":"text","text":"Don't ask: 'Would you use an app that does this?'"}]},{"at":63.41,"heading":"Questions & synthesis","items":[{"at":63.56,"kind":"text","text":"People are bad at predicting future behaviour."},{"at":70.65,"kind":"text","text":"Avoid leading questions; they suggest answers."},{"at":80.96,"kind":"text","text":"Group patterns; write a short problem statement."},{"at":85.76,"kind":"term","text":"Persona","detail":"Typical user from real research, not imagination."},{"at":91.65,"kind":"text","text":"5–8 interviews already show main patterns."}]},{"at":95.26,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":95.41,"kind":"text","text":"Worked example: leading → open"},{"at":97.1,"kind":"text","text":"Leading: 'Would you like a faster way to pay school fees?'"},{"at":101.77,"kind":"text","text":"Open: 'Last time you paid school fees—what was hardest?'"},{"at":106.38,"kind":"text","text":"Leading suggests the answer you want."}]},{"at":110.66,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":110.66,"kind":"question","text":"Which is the better interview question? A) Do you like our new design? B) Show me how you would book a ticket?"}]},{"at":121.63,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":121.78,"kind":"text","text":"Second question is better."},{"at":123.46,"kind":"text","text":"Shows behaviour; does not lead."}]},{"at":127.07,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":127.22,"kind":"wrong","text":"Ask friends/family only"},{"at":131.72,"kind":"wrong","text":"Ask for features, then build that list"}]},{"at":135.46,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":135.61,"kind":"wrong","text":"Leading questions; invented personas"},{"at":139.64,"kind":"tip","text":"Fix: real users, past behaviour, evidence-based personas."}]},{"at":146.47,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":146.62,"kind":"text","text":"Research before design: designer ≠ user."},{"at":151.69,"kind":"text","text":"Interviews, observation, surveys."},{"at":156.49,"kind":"text","text":"Patterns → problem statement → personas."},{"at":161.77,"kind":"tip","text":"Ask about the past, not the future."},{"at":165.51,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: keep learning."}]}],"check":{"at":121.28,"seconds":10,"question":"Which is the better interview question? A) Do you like our new design? B) Show me how you would book a ticket?","answer":"B: 'Show me how you would book a ticket?' It shows behaviour and does not lead."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}